Quad-kiting for a bard does indeed sound like quite a challenge, but possible.  I've done a... little bit... of quadding in my time and here's what i'd think would be "simplest" way to do it as a bard.<P>Druids quad using snare.  Not an option for a bard.  You could not twist snare on 4 mobs.  My take is that you would want to find 4 mobs and group them, at that point no twisting at all, just using selo.  Then find a flat area to kite them along.  Then get a little distance on them, turn backwards and face them, wait for them to close just out of melee range and twist selos/shout while running backwards.  I am able to keep ahead of mobs running backwards with SoW... you will have to slow down some to keep even.  I might even try de-equipping the drum so i'd be a little slower. <P>YMMV, tell me if it works!<p>[ January 12, 2002: Message edited by: Santerre ]<P>--------------------<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.vallisscortor.com/images/Santerre.gif"> Santerre: fashion-impaired Hierophant.
